Experiment 18: Docker Image Push to Docker Hub
Aim

To build a Docker image and push it to Docker Hub for image distribution.

Theory (Short)

Docker Hub is a cloud repository used to store and share Docker images.
Docker images can be pushed to Docker Hub and pulled from any system for deployment.
This helps in application distribution and version control.

Steps
Step 1: Login to Docker Hub
docker login

Enter:

Docker Hub username
Password
Step 2: Build Docker Image
docker build -t hello-docker .
Step 3: Tag Docker Image
docker tag hello-docker username/hello-docker

Example:

docker tag hello-docker harshitha/hello-docker
Step 4: Push Image to Docker Hub
docker push username/hello-docker

Example:

docker push harshitha/hello-docker
Step 5: Verify on Docker Hub

Go to:

https://hub.docker.com

Check repository and image.

Step 6: Pull Image from Docker Hub
docker pull username/hello-docker
